[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Heracles Software Requirements Specification for Backup Timer FW
UID: DHF-HRC-0017
METADATA:
  COMPONENT: backup-timers

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @grammar

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The purpose of this document is to provide Software Requirements Specifications for the Heracles
Backup Timer Firmware (FW).
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document describes all requirements of the Heracles Backup Timer FW.
The information in this document has been derived from the VoxelRay Heracles Product Requirements
Specification, as referenced in this document.

\*The term Software applies to both Software and Firmware systems.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Abbreviations and Definitions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
FW
  Firmware

MCU
  Microcontroller Unit

PRS
  Product Requirements Specification

SDP
  Software Development Plan

SRS
  Software Requirements Specification

SW
  Software
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Overview

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The Backup Timer firmware is used to interface with the main control firmware and count the registered
course of time once prompted. If the set period has elapsed, the timer firmware will trigger the timer
MCU to terminate the X-Ray emission.

The Backup Timer firmware runs on the Timer MCUs located on the main control board.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: References

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
EMS-WI-057-13: Generating Documents and Traceability Matrix Analysis in Ketryx WI

EMS-SOP-057: Software Design Control

DHF-HRC-0001, Rev. 1: Heracles Software Development Plan (SDP)

DHF-HRC-0002: VoxelRay Product Requirements Specification (PRS)
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: RQ-H1FWT-
TITLE: Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWT-1
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Timer Characteristics
STATEMENT: >>>
The timeout counter shall not continue to count once expired
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWT-2
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Timer Functionality
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall only allow the timer countdown to be reset if the timer is not running.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWT-3
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Timer Functionality
STATEMENT: >>>
The timer firmware shall be able to reset and clear the timeout counter.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWT-4
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Timer Functionality
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall clear any latched faults when the timer value is reset by the main control
microcontroller
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWT-5
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Communication
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall verify a checksum value to ensure valid communication with the main control
microcontroller
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWT-6
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Communication
STATEMENT: >>>
The timer firmware shall be able to send timer state information to the main control
microcontroller.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWT-9
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Timer Functionality
STATEMENT: >>>
The timer firmware shall set a latching fault status interlock signal if the timeout expires.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWT-10
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Timer Characteristics
STATEMENT: >>>
The timeout counter shall be able to have a maximum period of 2 minutes or more.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWT-11
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Timer Characteristics
STATEMENT: >>>
The timeout counter shall have a minimum resolution of 60 milliseconds or less.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWT-12
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Timer Functionality
STATEMENT: >>>
The timer firmware shall be able to start a timeout counter.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWT-13
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Timer Functionality
STATEMENT: >>>
The timer firmware shall be able to stop an ongoing timeout counter
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H1FWT-14
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Timer Functionality
STATEMENT: >>>
The timer firmware shall be able to program a timeout counter based on time parameters
received from the main microcontroller.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
